[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-WHITEBOARD-VIEW-PROGRAMS
TITLE: The programs
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: rows
STATEMENT: >>>
Four programs, run in this order by the task. A row's word says whether the program's code has landed; the node's own DEPTH says the same on the node, and the files it names are its File relations.

- The wireline reads the export, the grammar and the worktree and writes one payload per root, schema whiteboard-view/1, that the renderer and nothing else consumes. [LINK: MECH-VIEW-WIRELINE] [BUILT]
- The view check walks the tree under a root and reports, count first, the rules the parser does not check; its findings are also embedded in the payload. [LINK: MECH-VIEW-CHECK] [BUILT]
- The renderer splices one payload into a content-blind template and writes one self-contained page, refusing any schema it was not built for. [LINK: MECH-VIEW-RENDERER] [BUILT]
- One devenv task runs the export into a clean directory, then the check, the wireline and the renderer, and leaves the page and the payload under output/view/. [LINK: MECH-VIEW-TASK] [BUILT]
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
MECH-VIEW-CHECK:0000000
MECH-VIEW-RENDERER:0000000
MECH-VIEW-TASK:0000000
MECH-VIEW-WIRELINE:0000000
<<<
